{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_002, multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/resnet50/avgpool/weighted at 52.5% acc, 4.42 GPU hrs), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal combination is actually contributing over a single modality, or whether one modality dominates. config_005 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cheapest possible informative experiment—no RNA encoder, single profile (no aggregation), and resnet50 is a standard pretrained encoder—so expected cost is roughly 0.5–1.0 GPU hours, far below config_002. If image-only accuracy is close to 52.5%, RNA adds little value under this setup and future experiments should focus on image-encoder upgrades (e.g., ViT-L) or fusion refinements. If image-only is substantially lower (e.g., <40%), the RNA modality is clearly contributing and we should exploit that by testing RNA-encoder variants (scvi_n200, pca_n2000) and aggregation strategies. This single cheap experiment partitions the 8 remaining budget much more effectively than a second multimodal run, which would only give a small incremental signal on one sub-dimension while leaving the modality-contribution question unresolved."
}

